# Little kitchen in Russian: diminutives -ик, -очка, -онька
subtitle: "Кухонька, столик, чашечка: how Russian suffixes make a word small, dear or friendly — as Masha finds a name for Tom's restaurant."
tags: ["russian","russian diminutives","кухонька","russian suffixes","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/word-building","vocabulary/kitchen"]
thumb: "band \"Little kitchen, in Russian\" stamp \"-ОНЬКА\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"The simpler, the better in Russian: чем проще, тем лучше","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/211-russian-the-simpler-the-better.cast"}

